   "created_at": "2026-11-08T20:00:55Z",
   "updated_at": "2026-11-08T20:00:55Z",
   "body": "One correction to my earlier wording: I said that every wrong loopback key is always accepted. That was too broad. Current `identifyCaller` can reject a key Magpie recognizes as expired or revoked, even on loopback; arbitrary invalid and absent keys follow the local-caller path.\n\nYour report still identifies the key-verification limitation Anarlog saw, and your last reply said you would ask its team which endpoint it probes. I have not tested Anarlog or their probe. If you receive the endpoint or a failing request detail, please add it here; that will distinguish this client-side discovery behavior from any `/v1/models` handling gap. The existing trust boundary still intentionally keeps local agents keyless.",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
